IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc-definitions`
IMPORT `ccc13-logic`

-- ccc13-arson-property.l4 -- Criminal Code (Canada), Part XI: sections 433 to 443 (arson and other fires; other interference with property).
-- "property" is section 428's (the answer is taken as `the thing is property, by s 428`); "bodily harm" is the keel's `s 2 bodily harm`, called with its three facts;
-- "explosive substance" and "wreck" are the keel's `s 2 explosive substance` and `s 2 wreck`, called with the kind of thing. Reading of the answers as in ccc13-fraud.l4.

§ `Part XI -- sections 433 to 443`

§§ `Arson and Other Fires -- sections 433 to 436.1`

-- 433 Every person who intentionally or recklessly causes damage by fire or explosion to property, whether or not that person owns the property, is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for life where
-- (a) the person knows that or is reckless with respect to whether the property is inhabited or occupied; or (b) the fire or explosion causes bodily harm to another person.
-- src:7722 | Arson and Other Fires
-- src:7723 | Arson — disregard for human life
-- src:7724 | 433 Every person who intentionally or recklessly causes damage by fire or explosion to property, whether or not that person owns the property, is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for life where
-- src:7725 | (a) the person knows that or is reckless with respect to whether the property is inhabited or occupied; or
-- src:7726 | (b) the fire or explosion causes bodily harm to another person.
@ref s 433 (src:7722-7726)
GIVEN `the person intentionally or recklessly causes damage by fire or explosion to the property` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing is property, by s 428` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person knows that or is reckless with respect to whether the property is inhabited or occupied` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the fire or explosion causes a hurt or injury to another person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the injury interferes with the health or comfort of the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the injury is more than merely transient or trifling in nature` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 433 the conduct is the offence of arson -- disregard for human life` MEANS
    IF `the person intentionally or recklessly causes damage by fire or explosion to the property`
    THEN `ccc13 all of` (LIST `the thing is property, by s 428`
                            , `ccc13 any of` (LIST JUST `the person knows that or is reckless with respect to whether the property is inhabited or occupied`   -- (a)
                                                 , `s 2 bodily harm` `the fire or explosion causes a hurt or injury to another person` `the injury interferes with the health or comfort of the person` `the injury is more than merely transient or trifling in nature`))   -- (b)
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every person who intentionally or recklessly causes damage by fire or explosion to property, whether or not that person owns the property"

@ref s 433 (the punishments) (src:7722-7726)
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 433 the punishments` MEANS LIST
    (Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for life`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`)   -- limb 1: the limb the text states

@ref s 433 (the class of the offence) (src:7722-7726)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 433 the class of the offence` MEANS `an indictable offence`

-- src:7727 | Arson — damage to property
-- src:7728 | 434 Every person who intentionally or recklessly causes damage by fire or explosion to property that is not wholly owned by that person is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term not exceeding fourteen years.
@ref s 434 (src:7727-7728)
GIVEN `the person intentionally or recklessly causes damage by fire or explosion to the property` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing is property, by s 428` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the property is not wholly owned by that person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 434 the conduct is the offence of arson -- damage to property` MEANS
    IF `the person intentionally or recklessly causes damage by fire or explosion to the property` AND `the property is not wholly owned by that person`
    THEN `the thing is property, by s 428`
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every person who intentionally or recklessly causes damage by fire or explosion to property that is not wholly owned by that person"

@ref s 434 (the punishments) (src:7727-7728)
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 434 the punishments` MEANS LIST
    (Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `fourteen years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`)   -- limb 1: the limb the text states

@ref s 434 (the class of the offence) (src:7727-7728)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 434 the class of the offence` MEANS `an indictable offence`

-- src:7729 | Arson — own property
-- src:7730 | 434.1 Every person who intentionally or recklessly causes damage by fire or explosion to property that is owned, in whole or in part, by that person is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term not exceeding fourteen years, where the fire or explosion seriously threatens the health, safety or property of another person.
@ref s 434.1 (src:7729-7730)
GIVEN `the person intentionally or recklessly causes damage by fire or explosion to the property` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing is property, by s 428` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the property is owned, in whole or in part, by that person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the fire or explosion seriously threatens the health, safety or property of another person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 434.1 the conduct is the offence of arson -- own property` MEANS
    IF `the person intentionally or recklessly causes damage by fire or explosion to the property` AND `the property is owned, in whole or in part, by that person` AND `the fire or explosion seriously threatens the health, safety or property of another person`
    THEN `the thing is property, by s 428`
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every person who intentionally or recklessly causes damage by fire or explosion to property that is owned, in whole or in part, by that person"

@ref s 434.1 (the punishments) (src:7729-7730)
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 434.1 the punishments` MEANS LIST
    (Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `fourteen years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`)   -- limb 1: the limb the text states

@ref s 434.1 (the class of the offence) (src:7729-7730)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 434.1 the class of the offence` MEANS `an indictable offence`

-- 435 (1) Every person who, with intent to defraud any other person, causes damage by fire or explosion to property, whether or not that person owns, in whole or in part, the property, is guilty of (a) an indictable offence ... 10 years; or (b) summary conviction.
-- src:7731 | Arson for fraudulent purpose
-- src:7732 | 435 (1) Every person who, with intent to defraud any other person, causes damage by fire or explosion to property, whether or not that person owns, in whole or in part, the property, is guilty of
-- src:7733 | (a) an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than 10 years; or
-- src:7734 | (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref s 435(1) (src:7731-7734)
GIVEN `the person acts with intent to defraud any other person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person causes damage by fire or explosion to the property` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing is property, by s 428` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 435(1) the conduct is the offence of arson for a fraudulent purpose` MEANS
    IF `the person acts with intent to defraud any other person` AND `the person causes damage by fire or explosion to the property`
    THEN `the thing is property, by s 428`
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every person who, with intent to defraud any other person, causes damage by fire or explosion to property"

@ref s 435(1) (the punishments) (src:7731-7734)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 435(1) the punishments` MEANS LIST
    (Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `ten years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`)   -- limb 1: the limb the text states
    , `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`   -- limb 2: the text states no penalty: s 787(1)

@ref s 435(1) (the class of the offence) (src:7731-7734)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 435(1) the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

-- (2) Where a person is charged with an offence under subsection (1), the fact that the person was the holder of or was named as a beneficiary under a policy of fire insurance relating to the property ... is a fact from which intent to defraud may be inferred by the court.
-- src:7735 | Holder or beneficiary of fire insurance policy
-- src:7736 | (2) Where a person is charged with an offence under subsection (1), the fact that the person was the holder of or was named as a beneficiary under a policy of fire insurance relating to the property in respect of which the offence is alleged to have been committed is a fact from which intent to defraud may be inferred by the court.
@ref s 435(2) (src:7735-7736)
GIVEN `the person is charged with an offence under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person was the holder of or was named as a beneficiary under a policy of fire insurance relating to the property in respect of which the offence is alleged to have been committed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 435(2) intent to defraud may be inferred by the court from the fact of the fire insurance policy` MEANS
    IF NOT `the person is charged with an offence under subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a person is charged with an offence under subsection (1)"
    ELSE IF `the person was the holder of or was named as a beneficiary under a policy of fire insurance relating to the property in respect of which the offence is alleged to have been committed`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection names one fact from which intent may be inferred; it is silent about other facts

-- 436 (1) Every person who owns, in whole or in part, or controls property and who, as a result of a marked departure from the standard of care that a reasonably prudent person would use to prevent or control the spread of fires or to prevent explosions,
-- is a cause of a fire or explosion in that property that causes bodily harm to another person or damage to property is guilty of (a) ... five years; or (b) summary conviction.
-- src:7737 | Arson by negligence
-- src:7738 | 436 (1) Every person who owns, in whole or in part, or controls property and who, as a result of a marked departure from the standard of care that a reasonably prudent person would use to prevent or control the spread of fires or to prevent explosions, is a cause of a fire or explosion in that property that causes bodily harm to another person or damage to property is guilty of
-- src:7739 | (a) an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than five years; or
-- src:7740 | (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref s 436(1) (src:7737-7740)
GIVEN `the person owns, in whole or in part, or controls the property` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing is property, by s 428` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person is a cause of a fire or explosion in that property as a result of a marked departure from the standard of care that a reasonably prudent person would use to prevent or control the spread of fires or to prevent explosions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the fire or explosion causes a hurt or injury to another person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the injury interferes with the health or comfort of the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the injury is more than merely transient or trifling in nature` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the fire or explosion causes damage to property` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 436(1) the conduct is the offence of arson by negligence` MEANS
    IF `the person owns, in whole or in part, or controls the property` AND `the person is a cause of a fire or explosion in that property as a result of a marked departure from the standard of care that a reasonably prudent person would use to prevent or control the spread of fires or to prevent explosions`
    THEN `ccc13 all of` (LIST `the thing is property, by s 428`
                            , `ccc13 any of` (LIST `s 2 bodily harm` `the fire or explosion causes a hurt or injury to another person` `the injury interferes with the health or comfort of the person` `the injury is more than merely transient or trifling in nature`
                                                 , JUST `the fire or explosion causes damage to property`))
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every person who owns, in whole or in part, or controls property and who, as a result of a marked departure from the standard of care"

@ref s 436(1) (the punishments) (src:7737-7740)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 436(1) the punishments` MEANS LIST
    (Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `five years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`)   -- limb 1: the limb the text states
    , `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`   -- limb 2: the text states no penalty: s 787(1)

@ref s 436(1) (the class of the offence) (src:7737-7740)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 436(1) the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

-- src:7741 | Non-compliance with prevention laws
-- src:7742 | (2) Where a person is charged with an offence under subsection (1), the fact that the person has failed to comply with any law respecting the prevention or control of fires or explosions in the property is a fact from which a marked departure from the standard of care referred to in that subsection may be inferred by the court.
@ref s 436(2) (src:7741-7742)
GIVEN `the person is charged with an offence under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has failed to comply with any law respecting the prevention or control of fires or explosions in the property` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 436(2) a marked departure from the standard of care may be inferred by the court from the failure to comply with a law` MEANS
    IF NOT `the person is charged with an offence under subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a person is charged with an offence under subsection (1)"
    ELSE IF `the person has failed to comply with any law respecting the prevention or control of fires or explosions in the property`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection names one fact from which a marked departure may be inferred; it is silent about other facts

-- 436.1 Every person who possesses any incendiary material, incendiary device or explosive substance for the purpose of committing an offence under any of sections 433 to 436 is guilty of (a) ... five years; or (b) summary conviction.
-- src:7743 | Possession of incendiary material
-- src:7744 | 436.1 Every person who possesses any incendiary material, incendiary device or explosive substance for the purpose of committing an offence under any of sections 433 to 436 is guilty of
-- src:7745 | (a) an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than five years; or
-- src:7746 | (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref s 436.1 (src:7743-7746)
GIVEN `the person possesses the thing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing is an incendiary material or incendiary device` IS A BOOLEAN
      `what the thing is, as an explosive substance` IS A `s 2 explosive substance kind`
      `the purpose is to commit an offence under any of sections 433 to 436` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 436.1 the conduct is the offence of possession of incendiary material` MEANS
    IF `the person possesses the thing` AND `the purpose is to commit an offence under any of sections 433 to 436`
    THEN `ccc13 any of` (LIST JUST `the thing is an incendiary material or incendiary device`, `s 2 explosive substance` `what the thing is, as an explosive substance`)
         -- JUST FALSE when the thing is neither: FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "possesses any incendiary material, incendiary device or explosive substance"; NOTHING passes through from s 2 explosive substance (NOTHING-kind (includes))
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every person who possesses any incendiary material, incendiary device or explosive substance for the purpose of committing an offence under any of sections 433 to 436"

@ref s 436.1 (the punishments) (src:7743-7746)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 436.1 the punishments` MEANS LIST
    (Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `five years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`)   -- limb 1: the limb the text states
    , `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`   -- limb 2: the text states no penalty: s 787(1)

@ref s 436.1 (the class of the offence) (src:7743-7746)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 436.1 the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

§§ `Other Interference with Property -- sections 437 to 443`

-- src:7748 | Other Interference with Property
-- src:7749 | False alarm of fire
-- src:7750 | 437 Every one who wilfully, without reasonable cause, by outcry, ringing bells, using a fire alarm, telephone or telegraph, or in any other manner, makes or circulates or causes to be made or circulated an alarm of fire is guilty of
-- src:7751 | (a) an indictable offence and is liable to imprisonment for a term not exceeding two years; or
-- src:7752 | (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref s 437 (src:7748-7752)
GIVEN `the person acts wilfully` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person acts without reasonable cause` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person, by outcry, ringing bells, using a fire alarm, telephone or telegraph, or in any other manner, makes or circulates or causes to be made or circulated an alarm of fire` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 437 the conduct is the offence of a false alarm of fire` MEANS
    IF `the person acts wilfully` AND `the person acts without reasonable cause` AND `the person, by outcry, ringing bells, using a fire alarm, telephone or telegraph, or in any other manner, makes or circulates or causes to be made or circulated an alarm of fire`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every one who wilfully, without reasonable cause, by outcry, ringing bells, using a fire alarm, telephone or telegraph"

@ref s 437 (the punishments) (src:7748-7752)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 437 the punishments` MEANS LIST
    (Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `two years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`)   -- limb 1: the limb the text states
    , `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`   -- limb 2: the text states no penalty: s 787(1)

@ref s 437 (the class of the offence) (src:7748-7752)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 437 the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

-- src:7753 | Interfering with saving of wrecked vessel
-- src:7754 | 438 (1) Every person is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than five years or is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction who intentionally prevents or impedes, or who intentionally endeavours to prevent or impede,
-- src:7755 | (a) the saving of a vessel that is wrecked, stranded, abandoned or in distress, or
-- src:7756 | (b) a person who attempts to save a vessel that is wrecked, stranded, abandoned or in distress.
@ref s 438(1) (src:7753-7756)
GIVEN `the person acts intentionally` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person prevents or impedes, or endeavours to prevent or impede, the saving of a vessel that is wrecked, stranded, abandoned or in distress` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person prevents or impedes, or endeavours to prevent or impede, a person who attempts to save a vessel that is wrecked, stranded, abandoned or in distress` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 438(1) the conduct is the offence of interfering with the saving of a wrecked vessel` MEANS
    IF `the person acts intentionally` AND (   `the person prevents or impedes, or endeavours to prevent or impede, the saving of a vessel that is wrecked, stranded, abandoned or in distress`   -- (a)
                                           OR `the person prevents or impedes, or endeavours to prevent or impede, a person who attempts to save a vessel that is wrecked, stranded, abandoned or in distress`)   -- (b)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "who intentionally prevents or impedes, or who intentionally endeavours to prevent or impede"

@ref s 438(1) (the punishments) (src:7753-7756)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
