-- src:7765 | Removing natural bar without permission
-- src:7766 | 440 Every person who knowingly and without the written permission of the Minister of Transport removes any stone, wood, earth or other material that forms a natural bar necessary to the existence of a public harbour, or that forms a natural protection to such a bar, is guilty of
-- src:7767 | (a) an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than two years; or
-- src:7768 | (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref s 440 (src:7765-7768)
GIVEN `the person acts knowingly` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person acts without the written permission of the Minister of Transport` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person removes any stone, wood, earth or other material that forms a natural bar necessary to the existence of a public harbour, or that forms a natural protection to such a bar` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 440 the conduct is the offence of removing a natural bar without permission` MEANS
    IF `the person acts knowingly` AND `the person acts without the written permission of the Minister of Transport` AND `the person removes any stone, wood, earth or other material that forms a natural bar necessary to the existence of a public harbour, or that forms a natural protection to such a bar`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every person who knowingly and without the written permission of the Minister of Transport removes any stone, wood, earth or other material"

@ref s 440 (the punishments) (src:7765-7768)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
