-- (2) A land surveyor does not commit an offence under subsection (1) where, in his operations as a land surveyor, (a) he takes up, when necessary, a boundary mark mentioned in paragraph (1)(b) and carefully replaces it as it was before he took it up; or
-- (b) he takes up a boundary mark mentioned in paragraph (1)(b) in the course of surveying for a highway or other work that, when completed, will make it impossible or impracticable for that boundary mark to occupy its original position, and he establishes a permanent record of the original position sufficient to permit that position to be ascertained.
-- src:7779 | Saving provision
-- src:7780 | (2) A land surveyor does not commit an offence under subsection (1) where, in his operations as a land surveyor,
-- src:7781 | (a) he takes up, when necessary, a boundary mark mentioned in paragraph (1)(b) and carefully replaces it as it was before he took it up; or
-- src:7782 | (b) he takes up a boundary mark mentioned in paragraph (1)(b) in the course of surveying for a highway or other work that, when completed, will make it impossible or impracticable for that boundary mark to occupy its original position, and he establishes a permanent record of the original position sufficient to permit that position to be ascertained.
@ref s 443(2) (src:7779-7782)
GIVEN `the person is a land surveyor acting in their operations as a land surveyor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person takes up, when necessary, a boundary mark mentioned in paragraph (1)(b) and carefully replaces it as it was before taking it up` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person takes up a boundary mark mentioned in paragraph (1)(b) in the course of surveying for a highway or other work that, when completed, will make it impossible or impracticable for that boundary mark to occupy its original position` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person establishes a permanent record of the original position sufficient to permit that position to be ascertained` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 443(2) the land surveyor does not commit an offence under subsection (1)` MEANS
    IF `the person is a land surveyor acting in their operations as a land surveyor` AND (   `the person takes up, when necessary, a boundary mark mentioned in paragraph (1)(b) and carefully replaces it as it was before taking it up`   -- (a)
                                                                                         OR (`the person takes up a boundary mark mentioned in paragraph (1)(b) in the course of surveying for a highway or other work that, when completed, will make it impossible or impracticable for that boundary mark to occupy its original position` AND `the person establishes a permanent record of the original position sufficient to permit that position to be ascertained`))   -- (b)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A land surveyor does not commit an offence under subsection (1) where, in his operations as a land surveyor"; this subsection gives no saving on these facts

-- src:7775 | Interfering with international boundary marks, etc.
-- src:7776 | 443 (1) Every person is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than five years or is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction who intentionally pulls down, defaces, alters or removes
-- src:7777 | (a) a boundary mark lawfully placed to mark any international, provincial, county or municipal boundary, or
-- src:7778 | (b) a boundary mark lawfully placed by a land surveyor to mark any limit, boundary or angle of a concession, range, lot or parcel of land.
